   "block": {
    "type": "text",
    "label": "READING · PAULA'S SATURDAY",
    "html": "Paula lives with her husband and two children. Every Saturday morning, she goes to the supermarket near her house. She usually takes a big <b>cart</b> because she buys a lot of food for the week. She always starts in the fruit and vegetable section. Her children eat many apples and bananas, so she buys a lot of fruit. She doesn't buy much meat, because the family prefers fish and chicken. At the <b>checkout</b>, she pays with her card and puts everything in her bags.<br><br>Today is different. It's Saturday, but Paula isn't shopping with her children. They are playing football at school. Paula is walking down the <b>aisles</b> alone, and she is looking at her list. There isn't any bread on the <b>shelf</b>, so she is asking an employee for help. She is also buying some milk and a few eggs. The supermarket is very busy today: there are many people in the <b>line</b>, and Paula doesn't have much time. She needs to be home at 11 o'clock."
   }
